<i>America.</i>

742
00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:22.440
<i>How you gonna pay for that?</i>

743
00:52:22.500 --> 00:52:25.041
<i>Well, I hear you're doing pretty well
these days.</i>

744
00:52:25.125 --> 00:52:26.916
<i>He's a dickhead.</i>

745
00:52:28.500 --> 00:52:30.000
<i>Right, come on then.</i>

746
00:52:30.083 --> 00:52:32.625
<i>'Cause you look like shit, bruv,
I bought you something.</i>

747
00:52:32.708 --> 00:52:34.208
<i>Thought it might cheer you up.</i>

748
00:52:34.291 --> 00:52:35.291
<i>What?</i>

749
00:52:35.875 --> 00:52:37.625
<i>I love it when you two play.</i>

750
00:52:37.708 --> 00:52:39.333
<i>Right. Remember this?</i>

751
00:52:44.666 --> 00:52:46.083
<i>Ted, do you want me to...?</i>

752
00:52:58.125 --> 00:52:59.958
<i>Now, bring it home for me, bro.</i>

753
00:53:05.041 --> 00:53:06.041
<i>Aw.</i>

754
00:53:14.000 --> 00:53:15.083
<i>How long for?</i>

755
00:53:15.166 --> 00:53:17.708
<i>A while. It's a thirty-day tour.</i>

756
00:53:18.666 --> 00:53:20.333
<i>That'd be wicked.</i>

757
00:53:20.416 --> 00:53:22.041
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

758
00:53:22.125 --> 00:53:24.291
<i>This is your time, Vinnie.</i>

759
00:53:24.375 --> 00:53:27.291
<i>Maybe. I'll still be back
for your birthday though, yeah?</i>

760
00:53:27.375 --> 00:53:31.500
<i>- Oh, don't worry about it.
- No, bruv, I'll be there. I promise.</i>

761
00:53:31.583 --> 00:53:32.666
<i>All right?</i>

762
00:53:36.041 --> 00:53:38.208
<i>Oh, that would be lovely, Vinnie.</i>

763
00:53:41.125 --> 00:53:43.666
No. No, no.

764
00:53:45.333 --> 00:53:46.333
Oh.

765
00:53:51.583 --> 00:53:52.708
No.

766
00:54:10.750 --> 00:54:12.875
<i>Will you definitely be there Friday?</i>

767
00:54:13.583 --> 00:54:17.125
Yeah, Mum, I'll be there. I promise.

768
00:54:17.208 --> 00:54:22.583
<i>Yeah, we'd really like that.
He's... not doing so well.</i>

769
00:54:24.791 --> 00:54:27.471
Look, Mum. It's getting kind of
crazy here, but I'll see you Friday.

770
00:54:27.541 --> 00:54:29.458
<i>Okay, then. Bye.</i>

771
00:54:29.541 --> 00:54:31.666
- Excuse me. Thank you.
<i>- Love you.</i>

772
00:54:31.750 --> 00:54:33.791
All right, yeah, I love you. Bye. Bye.

773
00:54:33.875 --> 00:54:36.583
Guys, guys, guys, I need to let you
into a bit of a secret.

774
00:54:37.166 --> 00:54:38.875
This tour is not over.

775
00:54:38.958 --> 00:54:42.291
Due to popular demand,
we've got another ten more dates.

776
00:54:43.833 --> 00:54:45.500
Uh, when does that start, Dennis?

777
00:54:45.583 --> 00:54:47.833
First one is this Friday. Amsterdam.

778
00:54:48.416 --> 00:54:51.541
Um, is there any way
we could push that back a bit?

779
00:54:52.083 --> 00:54:54.250
What could be more important than this?

780
00:54:54.333 --> 00:54:55.375
Uh...

781
00:54:55.458 --> 00:54:57.916
No, it's just that I promised my, uh...

782
00:54:59.625 --> 00:55:01.583
I might need a couple of days to...

783
00:55:04.958 --> 00:55:06.625
Don't take too long.

784
00:55:06.708 --> 00:55:08.875
We might change our minds about you.

785
00:55:12.708 --> 00:55:13.750
Uh...

786
00:55:17.041 --> 00:55:18.041
Uh...

787
00:55:20.916 --> 00:55:25.125
Um, yeah. No, of course.
Yeah, I'm there. I'm there.

788
00:55:25.208 --> 00:55:26.625
Good man. Right.

789
00:55:26.708 --> 00:55:28.041
Right, champagne.

790
00:55:36.541 --> 00:55:40.125
<i>♪ Through the glory of life ♪</i>

791
00:55:40.208 --> 00:55:43.250
<i>♪ I was scattered on the floor ♪</i>

792
00:55:43.750 --> 00:55:48.583
<i>♪ Disappointed and sore ♪</i>

793
00:55:49.291 --> 00:55:53.000
<i>♪ And in my thoughts I have bled ♪</i>

794
00:55:53.083 --> 00:55:56.416
<i>♪ For the riddles I've been fed ♪</i>

795
00:55:56.500 --> 00:56:00.916
<i>♪ Another lie moves over ♪</i>

796
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:04.875
<i>♪ Oh, wild white horses ♪</i>

797
00:56:05.375 --> 00:56:09.250
<i>♪ They will take me away ♪</i>

798
00:56:10.166 --> 00:56:15.625
<i>♪ And my tenderness I feel ♪</i>

799
00:56:16.250 --> 00:56:22.083
<i>♪ Will send the dark underneath ♪</i>

800
00:56:22.166 --> 00:56:26.166
<i>♪ Will I follow? ♪</i>

801
00:56:26.250 --> 00:56:27.291
<i>Hello, love.</i>

802
00:56:29.291 --> 00:56:30.625
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

803
00:56:32.333 --> 00:56:33.333
<i>Ted...</i>

804
00:56:35.041 --> 00:56:36.083
<i>He's gone.</i>

805
00:56:37.583 --> 00:56:39.291
<i>He died this morning.</i>

806
00:56:52.666 --> 00:56:56.000
<i>♪ Wild white horses ♪</i>

807
00:56:56.666 --> 00:57:00.291
<i>♪ They will take me away ♪</i>

808
00:57:01.291 --> 00:57:06.875
<i>♪ And my tenderness I feel ♪</i>

809
00:57:07.416 --> 00:57:12.583
<i>♪ Will send the dark underneath ♪</i>

810
00:57:13.416 --> 00:57:18.708
<i>♪ Will I follow? ♪</i>

811
00:57:28.083 --> 00:57:30.708
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
we've arrived at Hastings.</i>

812
00:57:30.791 --> 00:57:33.125
<i>This service terminates here. Thank you.</i>

813
00:58:43.875 --> 00:58:45.083
Vinnie.

814
00:58:49.458 --> 00:58:50.750
About Ted's birthday...

815
00:58:52.333 --> 00:58:54.208
I'm sorry that I didn't make it down.

816
00:58:56.083 --> 00:58:57.125
I wanted to, but...

817
00:58:59.333 --> 00:59:00.625
You know how it is, innit?

818
00:59:05.083 --> 00:59:06.083
That's okay.

819
00:59:10.291 --> 00:59:13.125
I was thinking about that harmonica
Ted used to play, remember?

820
00:59:13.958 --> 00:59:15.458
Think it's still up in the loft?

821
00:59:18.166 --> 00:59:20.916
- It's just, I kind of wanted something...
- No, I don't know.

822
00:59:43.416 --> 00:59:44.416
Mum?

823
00:59:47.208 --> 00:59:48.333
Mum.

824
01:00:03.916 --> 01:00:05.250
Sure you don't know where it is?

825
01:00:05.333 --> 01:00:07.101
- I told you I don't know.
- I'll look myself.

826
01:00:07.125 --> 01:00:09.208
- Don't!
- Why not, Mum?

827
01:00:14.416 --> 01:00:16.916
Oh, you can't ambush me like this.

828
01:00:18.666 --> 01:00:20.166
I don't know where it is.

829
01:00:43.250 --> 01:00:44.250
Stevie?

830
01:00:47.000 --> 01:00:48.083
Stevie!

831
01:00:50.125 --> 01:00:53.250
Stevie, I'm talking to you.
Can you stop that, please?

832
01:01:25.041 --> 01:01:27.791
Can you talk to me, please? What's wrong?

833
01:01:38.208 --> 01:01:40.375
Okay, I know he was your friend.

834
01:01:41.416 --> 01:01:44.000
You don't need him to enjoy music, Stevie.

835
01:01:51.375 --> 01:01:52.625
I want to get better.

836
01:01:56.125 --> 01:01:57.125
Why?

837
01:01:57.583 --> 01:02:00.083
So I can go to the very good music school.

838
01:02:06.208 --> 01:02:07.208
Well...

839
01:02:09.791 --> 01:02:13.416
That's a really big deal, darling.
That's a really big deal.

840
01:02:14.625 --> 01:02:16.750
You know,
I think that might be a bit much.

841
01:02:19.375 --> 01:02:22.958
I think that would be a lot
for anybody to take on, okay?

842
01:02:23.750 --> 01:02:26.583
They wouldn't have
the care facilities you need.

843
01:02:26.666 --> 01:02:31.041
I don't need them.
I want to be like other musicians.

844
01:02:35.041 --> 01:02:37.333
You don't need to be like anyone else.

845
01:02:38.041 --> 01:02:40.208
Okay? You're perfect just as you are.

846
01:02:40.291 --> 01:02:41.750
No, I'm not, Mum.

847
01:02:47.291 --> 01:02:50.958
But if I study, you won't
have to look after me anymore.

848
01:02:51.541 --> 01:02:53.375
So you could do other things.

849
01:02:54.958 --> 01:02:58.125
I don't understand that.
What...? What do you mean?

850
01:02:58.625 --> 01:03:01.833
You stopped dancing
so you could look after me.

851
01:03:07.708 --> 01:03:09.041
Stevie, look at me.

852
01:03:11.500 --> 01:03:13.041
Look at me, Stevie.

853
01:03:14.500 --> 01:03:16.708
I really need you to hear this, okay?

854
01:03:17.291 --> 01:03:18.500
That is not true.

855
01:03:20.250 --> 01:03:22.958
I didn't want
to be part of that world anymore.

856
01:03:23.708 --> 01:03:26.000
I wanted you. Okay?

857
01:03:29.333 --> 01:03:32.625
I'm not a child.
I don't need you anymore.

858
01:05:01.041 --> 01:05:02.416
Hey, man. What can I get for you?

859
01:05:02.500 --> 01:05:03.875
You can get me a manager.

860
01:05:04.500 --> 01:05:06.250
- The manager?
- Yes.

861
01:05:06.333 --> 01:05:08.333
All right, just give me one sec.

862
01:05:11.291 --> 01:05:12.875
Hi, I'm the manager.

863
01:05:12.958 --> 01:05:15.083
I'm gonna have to give you this.

864
01:05:15.625 --> 01:05:19.833
We're looking for some cozy venues
to do a gig before we go on tour.

865
01:05:20.583 --> 01:05:23.500
I think we're probably gonna be
a bit too small for you, mate.

866
01:05:29.125 --> 01:05:30.166
All right, mate?

867
01:05:30.250 --> 01:05:31.541
Oh, hi, bouncer.

868
01:05:31.625 --> 01:05:32.625
Got any ID?

869
01:05:37.541 --> 01:05:39.500
I'm 18, nearly 19.

870
01:05:40.458 --> 01:05:42.083
All right, have a good night.

871
01:05:43.583 --> 01:05:44.583
Oh, good evening.

872
01:05:44.625 --> 01:05:46.208
I'd like to give you this.

873
01:05:47.291 --> 01:05:49.125
Not much effort in that, is there?

874
01:05:49.208 --> 01:05:54.000
We're, um, looking for some cozy venues
to do a gig before we go on tour.

875
01:05:54.083 --> 01:05:56.083
I don't think
this is the venue for you, lad.

876
01:05:56.166 --> 01:05:58.375
I recommend you take a look at that.

877
01:06:00.583 --> 01:06:01.875
This is your band, is it?

878
01:06:01.958 --> 01:06:04.958
Yes it is, with my man Vinnie D,
called The Tin Men.

879
01:06:05.666 --> 01:06:07.000
Nice.

880
01:06:07.083 --> 01:06:09.364
Yeah, like I said,
we're not really booking at the minute.

881
01:06:09.416 --> 01:06:11.166
Are you 100% sure about that?

882
01:06:17.208 --> 01:06:20.208
You know what? Give me your details
and I'll see what I can do.

883
01:06:20.791 --> 01:06:21.791
Awesome.

884
01:06:21.875 --> 01:06:22.875
Take a look at that.

885
01:06:22.916 --> 01:06:24.458
It's got Austin Roberts.

886
01:06:25.916 --> 01:06:27.416
It's gonna be bloody banging.

887
01:06:44.250 --> 01:06:45.291
Yeah?

888
01:06:45.375 --> 01:06:46.916
<i>Vince. It's me.</i>

889
01:06:48.166 --> 01:06:49.041
Stevie?

890
01:06:49.125 --> 01:06:50.625
I've got us a gig.

891
01:06:50.708 --> 01:06:51.750
Whoa.

892
01:06:52.625 --> 01:06:54.305
Slow down, man.
What are you talking about?

893
01:06:54.333 --> 01:06:57.291
The place is called Bar Star,
and the manager's called Marnie.

894
01:07:02.333 --> 01:07:05.375
Dude... listen, man. It's...

895
01:07:07.625 --> 01:07:08.625
It's over.

896
01:07:09.750 --> 01:07:11.458
<i>Bro, I'm sorry for what happened.</i>

897
01:07:11.541 --> 01:07:13.375
<i>I'm sorry for your mum as well, but...</i>

898
01:07:15.041 --> 01:07:17.125
She don't want me
hanging around you no more, and

899
01:07:18.041 --> 01:07:19.500
to be honest, I can see why.

900
01:07:20.083 --> 01:07:23.416
If you come to the music group,
you can say sorry to her face.

901
01:07:24.833 --> 01:07:26.767
- Stevie, mate...
<i>- Anyway, see you on Thursday. Bye.</i>

902
01:07:26.791 --> 01:07:28.125
No, no, no...

903
01:07:56.083 --> 01:07:57.833
Now, just ignore him, okay?

904
01:07:57.916 --> 01:07:59.833
Vince, please,
just leave us alone, all right?

905
01:07:59.916 --> 01:08:02.416
Why are you
lurking around in the car park?

906
01:08:02.500 --> 01:08:04.541
I'm not some kind of sex offender.

907
01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:07.916
I came to say sorry. That's all.

908
01:08:08.000 --> 01:08:11.666
Yeah, he's apologizing.
He's not a sex offender.

909
01:08:11.750 --> 01:08:12.750
Stevie.

910
01:08:13.250 --> 01:08:16.250
You know he put you in danger.
You do get that, right?

911
01:08:18.791 --> 01:08:19.916
Did you invite him?

912
01:08:21.333 --> 01:08:23.083
- Stevie!
- It's important.

913
01:08:23.166 --> 01:08:24.958
He didn't mean to do what he did.

914
01:08:25.041 --> 01:08:26.333
It's true. I didn't.

915
01:08:27.708 --> 01:08:29.583
Mum, please.

916
01:08:30.791 --> 01:08:33.333
I think you should hear him out.

917
01:08:40.333 --> 01:08:41.541
Go on then, what?

918
01:08:42.833 --> 01:08:43.916
I'm sorry.

919
01:08:45.250 --> 01:08:48.458
Both of you, I'm... I'm really sorry.

920
01:08:49.333 --> 01:08:51.666
I made it into a dangerous situation.

921
01:08:52.375 --> 01:08:53.458
That's on me.

922
01:08:56.541 --> 01:08:59.125
Mum, he was trying to protect me.

923
01:08:59.208 --> 01:09:01.625
Okay. Okay, we are ready to start.

924
01:09:02.625 --> 01:09:05.291
Come on. I think the class is starting.

925
01:09:16.333 --> 01:09:17.458
Today...

926
01:09:18.083 --> 01:09:19.833
Ah, Stevie!

927
01:09:19.916 --> 01:09:21.333
Ah, welcome.

928
01:09:21.416 --> 01:09:24.541
Join us. Vincent, long time.

929
01:09:24.625 --> 01:09:27.541
Take a seat. Quick, quick, quick,
quick, quick, quick, quick, quick.

930
01:09:27.625 --> 01:09:30.041
Today, we are going
to start with some singing.

931
01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:33.583
Who wants to be the heartbeat today?

932
01:09:36.291 --> 01:09:39.375
Vincent, you should be leader today.

933
01:09:39.958 --> 01:09:41.375
Find us our heartbeat.

934
01:09:41.458 --> 01:09:44.083
No. Trust me,
you don't want me doing that, man.

935
01:09:44.875 --> 01:09:46.458
Who wants Vincent to be leader?

936
01:09:46.541 --> 01:09:48.125
- Yeah!
- Yes, Dia.

937
01:09:48.208 --> 01:09:50.583
- Do we want Vincent to be leader?
- Yes, Dia.

938
01:09:50.666 --> 01:09:53.041
Uh-huh. The group has spoken.

939
01:09:59.791 --> 01:10:01.041
Ignite the circle.

940
01:10:06.250 --> 01:10:07.833
You want me to find the heartbeat?

941
01:10:09.291 --> 01:10:11.250
You can't live
without a heartbeat, can you?

942
01:10:12.916 --> 01:10:15.833
Except this guy. Am I right?

943
01:10:19.500 --> 01:10:21.375
Who's going to sing first then?

944
01:10:26.708 --> 01:10:27.708
Nadeera?

945
01:10:28.208 --> 01:10:31.166
I know you've got a beautiful song
in there waiting to come out.

946
01:10:32.125 --> 01:10:35.833
Go on, just... take your time.

947
01:10:44.083 --> 01:10:45.083
No?

948
01:10:48.416 --> 01:10:49.666
When you're ready, yeah?

949
01:10:52.666 --> 01:10:54.000
Come on. Who's next then?

950
01:10:54.958 --> 01:10:55.958
Saul?

951
01:10:58.458 --> 01:10:59.458
No?

952
01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:01.750
If you don't sing then...

953
01:11:01.833 --> 01:11:04.708
I'm going to have to serenade you
and we don't want that, do we?

954
01:11:06.166 --> 01:11:10.041
<i>♪ I see trees of green ♪</i>

955
01:11:11.833 --> 01:11:14.208
<i>♪ Red roses too ♪</i>

956
01:11:16.166 --> 01:11:18.208
<i>♪ I see them bloom ♪</i>

957
01:11:19.583 --> 01:11:21.458
<i>♪ For me and you ♪</i>

958
01:11:22.083 --> 01:11:27.250
<i>♪ And I think to myself ♪</i>

959
01:11:28.416 --> 01:11:31.750
<i>♪ What a wonderful world ♪</i>

960
01:11:33.416 --> 01:11:37.250
<i>♪ I see skies of blue ♪</i>

961
01:11:37.333 --> 01:11:40.250
<i>♪ And clouds of white ♪</i>

962
01:11:40.333 --> 01:11:42.958
<i>♪ The bright blessed day ♪</i>

963
01:11:43.041 --> 01:11:46.666
<i>♪ And the dark sacred night ♪</i>

964
01:11:46.750 --> 01:11:50.333
<i>♪ And I think to myself ♪</i>

965
01:11:50.416 --> 01:11:52.041
<i>♪ Mm, mm ♪</i>

966
01:11:52.125 --> 01:11:55.041
<i>♪ What a wonderful world ♪</i>

967
01:12:02.750 --> 01:12:04.750
That was really good, Nadeera.

968
01:12:08.500 --> 01:12:09.583
That was beautiful.

969
01:12:11.250 --> 01:12:12.458
Who's going next?

970
01:12:12.541 --> 01:12:13.916
- Me.
- Me.

971
01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:15.000
Me.

972
01:12:18.791 --> 01:12:21.333
She never sang like that for me, you know?

973
01:12:21.416 --> 01:12:23.000
You are good at this.

974
01:12:24.416 --> 01:12:25.583
I was just lucky, innit?

975
01:12:25.666 --> 01:12:28.166
Uh-huh. Listen.

976
01:12:29.375 --> 01:12:31.666
I'm looking for someone
to take over for me here.

977
01:12:32.208 --> 01:12:34.375
I want to put your name forward.

978
01:12:36.541 --> 01:12:39.250
- Me, teaching?
- My brother, when you got it, you got it.

979
01:12:44.500 --> 01:12:45.500
How much it pay?

980
01:12:48.041 --> 01:12:49.500
- The pay is okay.
- Yeah?

981
01:12:49.583 --> 01:12:51.916
But when you are good,
you can help a lot of people.

982
01:12:52.000 --> 01:12:54.458
The joy that comes
from teaching through music

983
01:12:54.541 --> 01:12:56.916
is better than any money or success.

984
01:13:00.458 --> 01:13:01.500
We'll talk later.

985
01:13:14.666 --> 01:13:17.916
Hey. You did well today.

986
01:13:18.000 --> 01:13:19.541
Very well, Vinnie D.

987
01:13:20.125 --> 01:13:21.125
Thanks.

988
01:13:50.166 --> 01:13:51.166
Hmm.

989
01:13:51.583 --> 01:13:54.916
You've been busy. Hopefully we'll
hear back from one of these soon.

990
01:13:55.750 --> 01:13:58.375
I kind of had a... offer as well, actually.

991
01:14:00.041 --> 01:14:02.458
Do you know anything about music therapy?

992
01:14:09.583 --> 01:14:11.041
Oh. Thanks, dude.

993
01:14:16.958 --> 01:14:18.583
You all right, Vinnie?

994
01:14:18.666 --> 01:14:20.500
Oh, you all right, yeah?

995
01:14:36.375 --> 01:14:37.541
Hello?

996
01:14:37.625 --> 01:14:39.416
Hey, bud. It's Austin.

997
01:14:39.500 --> 01:14:40.541
Oh, hey, man.

998
01:14:41.375 --> 01:14:43.250
I wasn't expecting your... call.

999
01:14:43.916 --> 01:14:45.583
I'm sorry about what happened last time.

1000
01:14:45.666 --> 01:14:48.375
Ah, don't be silly<i>,</i> man. It's fine.

1001
01:14:49.416 --> 01:14:50.791
To be honest, you had a point.

1002
01:14:50.875 --> 01:14:54.416
<i>I could've stepped up
for you more back when, uh...</i>

1003
01:14:57.500 --> 01:15:00.208
Anyway, I just got shown a video

1004
01:15:00.291 --> 01:15:02.916
<i>of you and your drummer
performing at The George.</i>

1005
01:15:03.000 --> 01:15:05.291
<i>The sound is really great, man.</i>

1006
01:15:06.166 --> 01:15:08.083
- Thanks, man.
<i>- Basically...</i>

1007
01:15:08.166 --> 01:15:10.875
No promises
because I gotta run it by Den, but...

1008
01:15:10.958 --> 01:15:13.833
you're in the mix to take
the supporting slot on my tour.

1009
01:15:13.916 --> 01:15:16.125
<i>If you're okay supporting me.</i>

1010
01:15:20.750 --> 01:15:22.166
<i>Would you be free</i>

1011
01:15:22.250 --> 01:15:24.333
to come down
to the studio on Friday for a chat?

1012
01:15:24.416 --> 01:15:28.333
Yeah, let me just, uh,
check the old schedule.

1013
01:15:37.166 --> 01:15:38.291
I think I can make that.

1014
01:15:40.875 --> 01:15:43.625
- All right. Brilliant.
- All right. See you then, mate.

1015
01:15:43.708 --> 01:15:45.416
All right. Cheers.

1016
01:15:45.500 --> 01:15:46.500
Nice one.

1017
01:15:49.625 --> 01:15:50.791
Oh my...

1018
01:16:02.250 --> 01:16:04.416
<i>♪ Don't you feel it growin' ♪</i>

1019
01:16:04.500 --> 01:16:06.125
<i>♪ Day by day... ♪</i>

1020
01:16:07.291 --> 01:16:09.000
Are we playing Bar Star first?

1021
01:16:09.083 --> 01:16:12.416
No, man. No, we're going on tour,
I want to write something new.

1022
01:16:14.208 --> 01:16:15.916
I can't even believe it.

1023
01:16:16.000 --> 01:16:18.916
You know, a month ago
I couldn't even finish off a verse.

1024
01:16:19.000 --> 01:16:20.375
Now we're The Tin Men.

1025
01:16:24.416 --> 01:16:26.416
Hey, we need to get
your mum on our side, though.

1026
01:16:26.500 --> 01:16:28.791
All right, I'll speak to her.

1027
01:16:28.875 --> 01:16:30.666
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

1028
01:16:30.750 --> 01:16:32.500
<i>♪ Listen to the music ♪</i>

1029
01:16:33.208 --> 01:16:35.333
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

1030
01:16:35.416 --> 01:16:37.166
<i>♪ Listen to the music ♪</i>

1031
01:16:37.791 --> 01:16:39.875
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

1032
01:16:39.958 --> 01:16:41.458
<i>♪ Listen to the music ♪</i>

1033
01:16:42.000 --> 01:16:47.166
<i>♪ All the time... ♪</i>

1034
01:16:50.791 --> 01:16:52.208
Right. No! Get out!

1035
01:16:52.291 --> 01:16:55.333
No, no, no, no.
Dave, you gave me a chance, right?

1036
01:16:55.416 --> 01:16:57.541
And I blew it. I'm sorry. I apologize.

1037
01:16:57.625 --> 01:16:59.625
Okay, give me 15 seconds
and I'll be out of here.

1038
01:16:59.708 --> 01:17:01.708
Mel, hi.

1039
01:17:02.625 --> 01:17:03.708
Hello.

1040
01:17:05.083 --> 01:17:06.958
Do you wanna go for a drink with me?

1041
01:17:07.041 --> 01:17:10.583
Not here. Not here.
Okay, somewhere else. Somewhere nicer.

1042
01:17:12.583 --> 01:17:14.208
Um... sure?

1043
01:17:15.791 --> 01:17:18.041
Cool. I'll be in touch.

1044
01:17:18.125 --> 01:17:20.958
All right. Dave, it's been emotional.

1045
01:17:21.041 --> 01:17:23.083
<i>♪ And you're feeling good to me ♪</i>

1046
01:17:23.583 --> 01:17:26.583
<i>♪ There ain't nothing we can't do or say ♪</i>

1047
01:17:27.416 --> 01:17:29.250
<i>♪ Feeling good ♪</i>

1048
01:17:29.833 --> 01:17:31.666
<i>♪ Feeling fine ♪</i>

1049
01:17:31.750 --> 01:17:33.625
<i>♪ Oh, baby ♪</i>

1050
01:17:33.708 --> 01:17:35.375
<i>♪ Let the music play ♪</i>

1051
01:17:36.416 --> 01:17:38.750
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

1052
01:17:38.833 --> 01:17:40.166
<i>♪ Listen to the music ♪</i>

1053
01:17:41.125 --> 01:17:43.250
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

1054
01:17:43.333 --> 01:17:44.916
<i>♪ Listen to the music ♪</i>

1055
01:17:45.416 --> 01:17:48.750
<i>♪ All the time ♪</i>

1056
01:17:50.625 --> 01:17:53.125
Everything's so small from up here, innit?

1057
01:17:54.583 --> 01:17:57.750
Hey. Great to see you again, Vinnie.

1058
01:17:58.500 --> 01:17:59.500
Yeah, man.

1059
01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:02.791
- When was the last time we...?
- Uh, Smash Hits Awards.

1060
01:18:02.875 --> 01:18:05.250
Fuck me, was it as long as that?

1061
01:18:06.125 --> 01:18:07.458
God.

1062
01:18:08.041 --> 01:18:08.875
Oh.

1063
01:18:08.958 --> 01:18:11.208
You look great. Hey.

1064
01:18:11.708 --> 01:18:17.125
Listen, we want this tour to be huge.
Yeah, we need a support act that

1065
01:18:17.208 --> 01:18:19.625
has some real meaning to the fans.

1066
01:18:21.500 --> 01:18:23.583
I want you to support me on my final tour.

1067
01:18:26.000 --> 01:18:27.000
No way?

1068
01:18:27.083 --> 01:18:30.875
Maybe at the end of your set,
I could come on stage and join you?

1069
01:18:30.958 --> 01:18:32.583
We could do one of the old hits.

1070
01:18:34.791 --> 01:18:36.708
Yeah.

1071
01:18:36.791 --> 01:18:38.166
Thank you.

1072
01:18:40.416 --> 01:18:41.416
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

1073
01:18:49.375 --> 01:18:50.458
What about Stevie?

1074
01:18:52.666 --> 01:18:54.541
- What, the drummer?
- Yeah.

1075
01:18:54.625 --> 01:18:57.791
I kind of need him
'cause we're The Tin Men, innit?

1076
01:18:57.875 --> 01:19:00.833
Yeah, I get it. He's a talent but, um...

1077
01:19:01.750 --> 01:19:03.833
Listen, we all know
what happened at that pub.

1078
01:19:03.916 --> 01:19:06.250
You can't be running
that kind of risk, Vince.

1079
01:19:06.333 --> 01:19:08.750
You can't have a special needs kid

1080
01:19:08.833 --> 01:19:12.083
with zero experience
going out drumming on the tour.

1081
01:19:12.166 --> 01:19:13.500
Steady on, mate.

1082
01:19:13.583 --> 01:19:16.000
I think he'd be all right
if he had a bit of support.

1083
01:19:16.666 --> 01:19:17.833
He's a good kid.

1084
01:19:17.916 --> 01:19:20.666
All I'm saying is this is about <i>you</i>.

1085
01:19:20.750 --> 01:19:24.166
I've got drummers
ten times his caliber, you know?

1086
01:19:24.250 --> 01:19:26.333
Ones that can handle the crowds.

1087
01:19:26.416 --> 01:19:29.666
You're going to be playing these songs
to a massive audience.

1088
01:19:29.750 --> 01:19:33.083
And we all know you've got
unfinished business up on that stage.

1089
01:19:33.166 --> 01:19:35.541
You might even get an album
off the back of it.

1090
01:19:37.250 --> 01:19:39.250
Don't tell me you don't want that, Vince.

1091
01:19:39.333 --> 01:19:42.416
No, of course I do. Of course.

1092
01:19:52.958 --> 01:19:57.208
Stevie. I had a meeting with Austin
and his manager Dennis yesterday.

1093
01:19:59.500 --> 01:20:01.208
Stevie, they asked me to...

1094
01:20:01.875 --> 01:20:03.791
They asked me to do the tour by myself.

1095
01:20:04.500 --> 01:20:05.666
On my own.

1096
01:20:10.416 --> 01:20:11.708
What about The Tin Men?

1097
01:20:14.916 --> 01:20:16.416
They just weren't up for it.

1098
01:20:17.083 --> 01:20:19.166
I think 'cause
me and Austin have got a history,

1099
01:20:19.875 --> 01:20:22.583
that's the only reason
they want me to go without you.

1100
01:20:22.666 --> 01:20:25.791
I really thought they were going
to take a punt on us, mate. I really did.

1101
01:20:25.875 --> 01:20:26.916
I tried.

1102
01:20:27.750 --> 01:20:29.333
But this industry is...

1103
01:20:29.416 --> 01:20:31.750
You only get one shot,
and that's if you're lucky.

1104
01:20:33.250 --> 01:20:35.416
It's a very great opportunity for you.

1105
01:20:36.708 --> 01:20:39.416
Yeah but, I don't know
if I'm going to do it yet.

1106
01:20:39.500 --> 01:20:41.041
I haven't decided, I just...

1107
01:20:43.000 --> 01:20:45.000
I said to them I'd think about it.

1108
01:20:46.583 --> 01:20:49.833
If you have a second shot,
then you really have to take it.

1109
01:20:50.958 --> 01:20:52.958
There will never be a third shot.

1110
01:20:58.291 --> 01:20:59.291
Thanks, man.

1111
01:21:03.041 --> 01:21:04.125
You really mean that?

1112
01:21:08.250 --> 01:21:09.916
It's my birthday next month.

1113
01:21:11.708 --> 01:21:15.000
That's wicked, man. What are you gonna do?

1114
01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:19.208
I'm going to go to a restaurant
for something to eat with my mum

1115
01:21:19.291 --> 01:21:20.625
after the music group.

1116
01:21:20.708 --> 01:21:22.541
- Nice.
- Do you want to come?

1117
01:21:23.583 --> 01:21:26.291
Yeah, man. Yeah, I'd love that.

1118
01:21:27.916 --> 01:21:29.291
It sounds like a plan.

1119
01:21:31.583 --> 01:21:32.750
Goodbye, Vince.

1120
01:21:33.375 --> 01:21:36.708
You going?
I'll see you later, Stevie, yeah?

1121
01:21:52.916 --> 01:21:54.250
What happened, Stevie?

1122
01:21:57.125 --> 01:21:59.291
I need to practice, Mum.

1123
01:22:00.375 --> 01:22:01.500
Please.

1124
01:22:05.000 --> 01:22:06.000
Okay.

1125
01:22:54.500 --> 01:22:58.791
<i>♪ So whether music or madness ♪</i>

1126
01:23:01.291 --> 01:23:04.208
<i>♪ We live by one of the two ♪</i>

1127
01:23:05.041 --> 01:23:07.583
<i>♪ By one of the two ♪</i>

1128
01:23:08.083 --> 01:23:14.208
<i>♪ So go on
Fill your heart up with gladness ♪</i>

1129
01:23:15.000 --> 01:23:17.500
<i>♪ Not a moment too soon ♪</i>

1130
01:23:18.375 --> 01:23:21.000
<i>♪ Not a moment too soon ♪</i>

1131
01:23:21.708 --> 01:23:28.041
<i>♪ Should we ration the reasons ♪</i>

1132
01:23:28.125 --> 01:23:30.875
<i>♪ To the child to ignore? ♪</i>

1133
01:23:31.833 --> 01:23:34.791
<i>♪ Of this, I've never been sure... ♪</i>

1134
01:23:34.875 --> 01:23:38.791
Okay, my friends.
Let's start. Are we ready?

1135
01:23:38.875 --> 01:23:41.541
Where's Stevie? Where's Vince.

1136
01:23:42.833 --> 01:23:44.750
Not everyone is here today.

1137
01:23:44.833 --> 01:23:46.375
But we'll manage.

1138
01:23:46.458 --> 01:23:48.375
<i>♪ To the form ♪</i>

1139
01:23:48.458 --> 01:23:55.250
<i>♪ Mm, mm, mm ♪</i>

1140
01:23:56.916 --> 01:23:59.458
<i>♪ Mm, mm... ♪</i>

1141
01:23:59.541 --> 01:24:00.583
What's this?

1142
01:24:00.666 --> 01:24:01.666
Do you mind?

1143
01:24:03.583 --> 01:24:04.583
Oh. Okay.

1144
01:24:06.083 --> 01:24:08.208
You know, I saw Nadeera's mum today.

1145
01:24:08.750 --> 01:24:11.416
Everybody misses you
at music group, she says.

1146
01:24:12.750 --> 01:24:15.125
You know, I still don't understand
why you're not going.

1147
01:24:16.375 --> 01:24:18.833
Nah... It's not the same anymore.

1148
01:24:19.916 --> 01:24:22.500
<i>♪ You're made of ♪</i>

1149
01:24:22.583 --> 01:24:25.083
<i>♪ And that's nothing to fear ♪</i>

1150
01:24:25.750 --> 01:24:28.500
<i>♪ No, it's nothing, my dear ♪</i>

1151
01:24:28.583 --> 01:24:32.375
<i>♪ But how do I know
What you're thinking? ♪</i>

1152
01:24:36.250 --> 01:24:38.083
Sure you don't want me to come with you?

1153
01:24:38.833 --> 01:24:41.541
- Definitely don't need your sticks?
- No, I'm all right. Thank you.

1154
01:24:41.625 --> 01:24:43.041
I can do this on my own.

1155
01:24:43.541 --> 01:24:46.041
Just have fun. Have a great day,
and I'll see you at home.

1156
01:24:46.125 --> 01:24:50.208
Yeah, okay. Just... turn around. Okay. Go.

1157
01:24:51.625 --> 01:24:52.833
I love you.

1158
01:24:52.916 --> 01:24:57.000
<i>♪ Singing, "Give me some more" ♪</i>

1159
01:24:59.625 --> 01:25:03.500
<i>♪ Oh, fever to the form... ♪</i>

1160
01:25:03.583 --> 01:25:06.791
<i>This is our state-of-the-art
percussion department.</i>

1161
01:25:06.875 --> 01:25:08.458
Come this way.

1162
01:25:09.958 --> 01:25:12.666
<i>♪ Singing, "Give me some more" ♪</i>

1163
01:25:13.375 --> 01:25:19.750
<i>♪ 'Cause you were never empty ♪</i>

1164
01:25:19.833 --> 01:25:23.041
<i>♪ And we've been here before ♪</i>

1165
01:25:23.125 --> 01:25:26.833
<i>♪ Yes, we've been here before ♪</i>

1166
01:25:26.916 --> 01:25:28.916
<i>♪ But now there's always plenty... ♪</i>

1167
01:25:29.000 --> 01:25:32.541
This is our world-class concert hall,

1168
01:25:32.625 --> 01:25:36.166
which has played host to some
of the finest musicians in the world.

1169
01:25:36.250 --> 01:25:38.791
- Did Jack DeJohnette play here?
- That's correct.

1170
01:25:38.875 --> 01:25:40.875
Right over there.

1171
01:25:47.958 --> 01:25:53.625
<i>♪ Mm, mm, mm, mm, mm ♪</i>

1172
01:25:57.708 --> 01:26:00.583
<i>♪ Mm, mm ♪</i>

1173
01:26:02.000 --> 01:26:03.000
I love you, Mum.

1174
01:26:04.583 --> 01:26:05.958
I love you too, baby.

1175
01:26:28.583 --> 01:26:29.708
Amber.

1176
01:26:30.208 --> 01:26:31.208
Hello.

1177
01:26:32.291 --> 01:26:33.291
You okay?

1178
01:26:34.583 --> 01:26:35.750
Can we talk?

1179
01:26:35.833 --> 01:26:38.041
Yeah. Yeah, come in.

1180
01:26:38.125 --> 01:26:39.208
Thanks.

1181
01:26:41.333 --> 01:26:42.333
How you been?

1182
01:26:43.375 --> 01:26:44.916
- I'm okay.
- Yeah?

1183
01:26:46.625 --> 01:26:48.833
How's Stevie? How's he doing?

1184
01:26:50.000 --> 01:26:55.291
Yeah. You know,
he's going to need some time, I think.

1185
01:26:55.375 --> 01:27:00.291
Yeah. It was a...
a bombshell for both of us.

1186
01:27:01.291 --> 01:27:04.125
Oh yeah? Going on tour
with Austin Roberts.

1187
01:27:04.208 --> 01:27:05.791
You must be devastated.

1188
01:27:05.875 --> 01:27:07.583
I wanted it to be with Stevie.

1189
01:27:15.500 --> 01:27:17.958
You must be relieved
it's all over now though, hey?

1190
01:27:18.916 --> 01:27:20.083
Not really.

1191
01:27:20.875 --> 01:27:23.666
Come on, now.
I know you've always hated me.

1192
01:27:24.875 --> 01:27:26.333
I've never hated you.

1193
01:27:28.708 --> 01:27:29.708
Look.

1194
01:27:30.583 --> 01:27:32.791
You have managed
to bring out something in him

1195
01:27:32.875 --> 01:27:35.166
that no one else has been able to do.

1196
01:27:36.833 --> 01:27:38.375
It's actually really annoying.

1197
01:27:42.833 --> 01:27:44.833
I saw how much you meant to him.

1198
01:27:46.250 --> 01:27:47.708
It made me really happy.

1199
01:27:50.291 --> 01:27:52.666
Why do you think I agreed to the gig?

1200
01:27:54.500 --> 01:27:56.250
I don't really know, really.

1201
01:27:56.333 --> 01:27:59.375
Because I saw
how bloody brilliant The Tin Men were.

1202
01:28:02.375 --> 01:28:04.833
You know, these days I look at Stevie

1203
01:28:06.416 --> 01:28:11.875
and I see these flashes
of the man he could be.

1204
01:28:12.458 --> 01:28:13.458
You know?

1205
01:28:16.125 --> 01:28:17.791
I was holding him back.

1206
01:28:19.250 --> 01:28:21.083
He was sort of stuck, you know.

1207
01:28:25.208 --> 01:28:26.208
Yeah.

1208
01:28:28.500 --> 01:28:29.375
But...

1209
01:28:29.458 --> 01:28:31.500
I can't just stand by

1210
01:28:31.583 --> 01:28:34.666
and watch his head get filled
with empty promises. I can't do that.

1211
01:28:36.750 --> 01:28:39.791
He was never in it
to make a name for himself, Vince.

1212
01:28:40.750 --> 01:28:41.791
You were.

1213
01:28:43.291 --> 01:28:45.166
All he ever wanted was a friend.

1214
01:28:47.791 --> 01:28:49.250
I was his friend.

1215
01:28:49.333 --> 01:28:52.583
I am... his friend.

1216
01:28:59.458 --> 01:29:00.833
Should have been both of us.

1217
01:29:03.541 --> 01:29:04.541
But it's not.

1218
01:29:05.833 --> 01:29:08.458
It's Vince Denham on tour and...

1219
01:29:09.583 --> 01:29:10.833
That's fine.

1220
01:29:13.583 --> 01:29:14.583
I shouldn't go.

1221
01:29:19.750 --> 01:29:21.958
- Don't say that.
- No, I shouldn't do it.

1222
01:29:22.041 --> 01:29:26.166
Vince,
you've wanted this for so long.

1223
01:29:27.958 --> 01:29:29.291
You really deserve it.

1224
01:29:39.416 --> 01:29:40.791
But I need you out of his life.

1225
01:29:45.541 --> 01:29:49.666
What about his birthday? He asked me if I...

1226
01:29:50.416 --> 01:29:51.500
I'm sorry.

1227
01:29:52.958 --> 01:29:56.250
I hope this goes well for you.
I really do.

1228
01:29:57.333 --> 01:29:59.083
But I've got to draw the line here.

1229
01:29:59.666 --> 01:30:01.708
You understand what I'm saying, don't you?

1230
01:30:05.083 --> 01:30:07.083
He needs to find his own path now.

1231
01:30:17.291 --> 01:30:18.333
Yeah.

1232
